<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Assembly of the Year XIII</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1813">1813</a>–<a href="/years/1815">1815</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Assembly of Year XIII</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Assembly of the Year XIII was the general constituent assembly of the United Provinces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a>, which met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> from 1813. Although it did not declare independence, it adopted a national anthem and coat of arms, abolished noble titles, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-inquisition">Inquisition</a> and torture, and declared children born to enslaved mothers free. Its rejection of the delegates from the Eastern Province deepened the split with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-gervasio-artigas">José Gervasio Artigas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/assembly-of-the-year-xiii.jpg" alt="Assembly of the Year XIII" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Asamblea_del_a%C3%B1o_XIII.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
